{"record": "turn", "turn": 4, "seconds": 7.533, "response_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "stop_reason": "tool_use", "stop_details": null, "blocks": ["thinking", "thinking", "tool_use"], "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 5716}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 5716, "cache_read_input_tokens": 7771, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 1152, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 658}, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "tools": [{"id": "toolu_01NjBGFL21aP9QkBZyD5b6sY", "name": "submit_answer", "arguments": {"answer": "arXiv:2610.26648v1 gives an integrated J_ann = 8.86×10^22 GeV^2 cm^-5 over its fitting region, the 40°×40° square with |b|>2°, which has ΔΩ = 0.429 sr (generalized NFW, γ=1.2, r_s=20 kpc, ρ(r0)=0.4 GeV/cm^3, r0=8.5 kpc). Elor, Rodd & Slatyer (1503.01773v2) quote an averaged J_norm ≈ 2.0618×10^23 GeV^2 cm^-5 over the ROI |l|≤20°, 2°≤|b|≤20°, i.e. the same region, with the same NFW parameters. Dividing the integrated value by the solid angle: 8.86×10^22/0.429 ≈ 2.07×10^23 GeV^2 cm^-5, which agrees with 2.06×10^23 to about 0.2%. The division is my own calculation; 2610.26648v1 does not state an averaged value.", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "3.6"}, {"arxiv_id": "1503.01773v2", "section_id": "2"}]}, "status": "answer", "error_kind": null, "seconds": 0.0}]}
{"record": "end", "run_id": "20261117T083646Z_eval-11_staged_c46c", "reason": "answered", "detail": "", "answer": {"answer": "arXiv:2610.26648v1 gives an integrated J_ann = 8.86×10^22 GeV^2 cm^-5 over its fitting region, the 40°×40° square with |b|>2°, which has ΔΩ = 0.429 sr (generalized NFW, γ=1.2, r_s=20 kpc, ρ(r0)=0.4 GeV/cm^3, r0=8.5 kpc). Elor, Rodd & Slatyer (1503.01773v2) quote an averaged J_norm ≈ 2.0618×10^23 GeV^2 cm^-5 over the ROI |l|≤20°, 2°≤|b|≤20°, i.e. the same region, with the same NFW parameters. Dividing the integrated value by the solid angle: 8.86×10^22/0.429 ≈ 2.07×10^23 GeV^2 cm^-5, which agrees with 2.06×10^23 to about 0.2%. The division is my own calculation; 2610.26648v1 does not state an averaged value.", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "3.6"}, {"arxiv_id": "1503.01773v2", "section_id": "2"}]}, "turns": 4, "seconds": 12.585, "tool_calls": 5, "tool_result_chars": 24488, "input_tokens": 10, "output_tokens": 1521, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 13487, "cache_read_input_tokens": 14081, "parser_versions": ["4"], "response_models": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"], "ended_at": "2026-11-17T08:36:58+00:00"}
